comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-23T13:57:18.042Z","harness:claude-code","Scope addition from the sixth Codex pass on PR #1772 (2026-11-23, P3, not reproduced here): schema add-field treats an explicit cliFlag that normalizes to nothing ('--') as omitted and silently drops a whitespace-only alias (normalizeAddFieldInput in src/core/schema/fields-file.ts), so the command succeeds with the default flag or without the requested alias, while the inline settings writer refuses the same spelling with schema_field_flag_invalid. Decide whether add-field should refuse an explicitly supplied empty spelling the same way; the same pass raised the duplicate inline definition and negated mutation flag cases again, both already in this item.\n"
